<title>EGYPT: Yield rises on Egyptian 91-day T-bills. [CORRECTED 05:09 GMT]</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Egyptian 91-day T-bills. [CORRECTED 05:09 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills rose (corrects from fell) to 8.888 percent on Thursday from 8.808 percent at the previous auction on May 21.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt had asked for 1.3 billion pounds and accepted bids for 1,387.025 million, Bills worth 986.125 million pounds mature today.</p>
<p>The Central Bank announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Aug 28, 1997 (Aug 21, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 8.888 percent (8.808)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 1,387.025 million (1,410.425 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,647.800 million (2,690.450 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.002-8.998 percent (8.499-8.838)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.002-9.203 percent (8.499-9.888)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 109 (91)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 140 (219)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1/</p>
